WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.570
A cottage room.

2
00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:04.130
A small child sits on a stool.

3
00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:08.760
His grandad leans back against the
wall, his walking stick beside him.

4
00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:13.120
The child does all the talking:
"I'm vex'd to see you, dad."

5
00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:18.040
He chats, he promises, he tells
stories of foxes and knights.

6
00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:20.510
The old man never answers.

7
00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:23.430
It's such a simple, chatty poem.

8
00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:26.870
So why does its last line hurt so much?

9
00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.260
In this mission, you'll
meet Joanna Baillie,

10
00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:32.280
and a child who talks
to a silent listener.

11
00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:35.270
You'll gather the signs of
illness the child describes,

12
00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:37.690
from the stick to the hollow cheeks.

13
00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:42.980
And you'll hear the child's promises,
like "I'll lead you kindly by the hand:"

14
00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:46.840
Your mission: explain
why the last line hurts.
